+# Contributing to Loru
+
+Thanks for helping improve Loru. The project keeps its smoke path offline and CPU-friendly, so contributions should preserve deterministic local tests and avoid requiring network access for CI.
+
+## Setup
+
+Loru requires Python 3.11+.
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/mergeos-bounties/Loru.git
+cd Loru
+python -m venv .venv
+source .venv/bin/activate  # Windows PowerShell: .\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
+pip install -e ".[dev]"
+```
+
+Install optional extras only when your change needs them, for example `.[gui]`, `.[api]`, `.[voice]`, or `.[torch]`.
+
+## Before opening a PR
+
+Run the core checks from the repository root:
+
+```bash
+ruff check src tests
+pytest -q
+loru demo
+```
+
+If you changed the desktop GUI, also install `.[gui]` and exercise `loru-gui`. If you changed optional API/voice/torch behavior, test with the matching extra installed and keep the base install working.
+
+## PR checklist
+
+- [ ] Keep the change focused and link the issue it resolves.
+- [ ] Add or update tests for behavior changes.
+- [ ] `ruff check src tests` passes.
+- [ ] `pytest -q` passes.
+- [ ] `loru demo` still completes for changes touching the core pipeline.
+- [ ] New datasets include license/consent notes; do not commit private recordings or PII.
+- [ ] Optional dependencies fail gracefully when the corresponding extra is not installed.
+- [ ] User-facing behavior or commands are reflected in README/docs where relevant.
+- [ ] PR description includes the evidence required by `docs/BOUNTY.md` when claiming a bounty.
+
+## Good first issues and MergeOS bounties
+
+Look for issues labeled [`good first issue`](https://github.com/mergeos-bounties/Loru/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+label%3A%22good+first+issue%22) or [`bounty`](https://github.com/mergeos-bounties/Loru/issues?q=is%3Aissue+is%3Aopen+label%3Abounty).
+
+Bounty contributors must follow the claim flow **before starting work**. The canonical repository instructions are in [`docs/BOUNTY.md`](docs/BOUNTY.md): follow/star the listed MergeOS repositories, claim the Loru issue, link it in MergeOS Claim Token #1, then open a focused PR to `master` with `Fixes #N` and the required evidence.
+
+The issue title is not settlement evidence. MRG credit is issued only after maintainer review and merge under the bounty policy.
+
+## Scope and conduct
+
+Keep contributions respectful, accessible, and privacy-conscious. Sign-language data can be personally identifying; prefer synthetic fixtures for tests and document consent/licensing for real-world datasets.
